          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3 How to Test Different Components of Food?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.147,
            0.883,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us find out which nutrients are present in various food items."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.188,
            0.885,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some nutrients like "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "starch",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (a type of carbohydrate), fat and protein can be detected using fairly simple tests, while others can be detected only in a well-equipped laboratory. Let us explore how we can detect the presence of starch, fat and protein in some food items."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.301,
            0.489,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3.1 Test for starch"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.341,
            0.586,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.5: Let us investigate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.374,
            0.885,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a small quantity of the food items such as a slice of potato, cucumber, bread, some boiled rice, boiled gram, crushed peanuts, oil, butter and crushed coconut. You can take other food items too for testing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.384,
            0.461,
            0.77,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.384,
                0.461,
                0.77,
                0.685
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.313,
                0.69,
                0.823,
                0.709
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 3.7: Testing for the presence of starch in various food items"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.721,
            0.842,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Place a small piece of each item on a separate dish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.747,
            0.883,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "With the help of a dropper, put 2–3 drops of diluted iodine solution on each food item (Fig. 3.7)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.796,
            0.884,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Observe if there are any changes in the colour of the food items. Have they turned blue-black? Record your observations in Table 3.3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.861,
            0.813,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A blue-black colour indicates the presence of starch."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
